WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.360
We know how to shift a row.

00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:04.720
Now reverse the order in which the cyclic positions are read.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:08.900
If h of X has coefficients h zero through h n minus

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:13.120
one, define h star by replacing X with X inverse.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:17.780
Since X inverse equals X to the n minus one, the result

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:19.340
stays in the same group ring.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:22.520
The constant coefficient stays fixed.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.980
The remaining positions are read backward.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:31.980
Use four generic coefficients to see this clearly: a, b, c, d

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:35.540
becomes a, d, c, b.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:40.380
The coefficients keep their values; only their cyclic positions reverse.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:47.440
Return to our original polynomial, negative one plus X plus X squared

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.440
plus X cubed.

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:55.680
Its star is negative one plus X inverse plus X to the

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:58.770
negative two plus X to the negative three.

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:01.620
Reduce exponents modulo four.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:07.700
The result is negative one plus X cubed plus X squared plus

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:10.240
X, which is our original polynomial.

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:15.380
This particular row is unchanged because its final three coefficients are equal.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:18.520
Why is star well defined?

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:23.100
The rule defining our group ring is X to the n equals

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:23.740
one.

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:27.280
Its inverse also has nth power one.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:32.660
Replacing X by X inverse therefore respects that defining relation, so equal

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:34.560
ring elements still have equal stars.

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:40.120
Reverse twice, and every position returns to where it started.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:43.100
The star of h star is h.

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:47.160
Replacing X by X inverse also respects multiplication.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:52.320
In this commutative group ring, the star of f times g is

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:54.420
f star times g star.

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:57.380
Thus star is an involution of the ring.

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:02.060
Remember what star does: it reverses cyclic positions.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:07.480
It neither negates the coefficients nor takes the reciprocal of the polynomial.

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:12.940
We introduced it because multiplying h by its reversal will encode every

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:16.020
cyclic dot product in a single polynomial.
